      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "T'ANG Hsien-tsu 湯顯祖 (T. 義仍, H. 若士, 海若, 清遠道人), 1550–1616, dramatist, contemporary of Shakespeare, was a native of Lin-ch'uan, Kiangsu. A chin-shih of 1583, he was appointed to a minor post in the government at Nanking, and after two years was promoted to a secretaryship in the Board of Ceremonies.",
